  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRIMARY EDUCATION FOR DISADVANTAGED CHILDREN PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to improve access to primary school and the quality of education for disadvantaged girls and boys. Disadvantaged children are broadly defined as school-aged children who are not enrolled or are at risk of not completing their primary education; children who attend schools that do no meet fundamental quality standards; and disabled children or children from other highly vulnerable groups, such as street children, migrant children or girls in certain ethnic minority areas.</narrative>
  </description>
